{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00630",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 12.74,
      "duration_seconds": 12.13,
      "text": "Hello there, doctor. Lovely to meet you. I'm only here because my daughter nagged me, she says I get puffed out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.78,
      "end_seconds": 20.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Well, I'm glad she nagged. What does she mean by puffed out? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.41,
      "end_seconds": 39.88,
      "duration_seconds": 17.47,
      "text": "It's only when I carry my shopping, you see. Up the hill from the Co-op, two bags, and by the top I've got to stop and catch my breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.92,
      "end_seconds": 45.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "How long has that been happening, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.27,
      "end_seconds": 57.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "Oh, a few months, maybe since the spring. I thought I was just getting old. I'm sixty-eight, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.66,
      "end_seconds": 65.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "That's not old. Does it ever happen when you're walking without the bags?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.98,
      "end_seconds": 83.87,
      "duration_seconds": 15.89,
      "text": "Not really, no. Only when I'm laden. I did the Pennine Way in my forties, you know, so I like to think I've got a bit of stamina. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.8,
      "end_seconds": 91.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "I'm sure you have. Any chest pain, or tightness, when you're puffed out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.16,
      "end_seconds": 97.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "No pain, no. Just short of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.04,
      "end_seconds": 107.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "And any swelling in your ankles, or waking up at night breathless?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.12,
      "end_seconds": 116.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "No, I sleep like a log. My ankles are the same as ever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.37,
      "end_seconds": 122.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Good. What tablets are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.32,
      "end_seconds": 137.84,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "Bisoprolol, 2.5 mg once a day, and ramipril, 5 mg once a day. They're for my blood pressure, I think. Or my heart? One of the two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.62,
      "end_seconds": 149.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.72,
      "text": "Both are good for the heart and the blood pressure, so you're right either way. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.11,
      "end_seconds": 153.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Ha! Good, I wasn't sure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.06,
      "end_seconds": 157.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.58,
      "end_seconds": 167.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "I gave up in 1998, thank goodness. Twenty a day I was smoking, if you can believe it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.26,
      "end_seconds": 174.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Well done. Let me check your pulse and oxygen first. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.99,
      "end_seconds": 182.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Do you want my wrist or my finger? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.12,
      "end_seconds": 199.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Just the finger, thanks. Pulse 66 and oxygen 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.68,
      "end_seconds": 207.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Is that good for a man of my age? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.06,
      "end_seconds": 214.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "It's excellent. Now I'll listen to your heart and lungs. Breathe normally. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.76,
      "end_seconds": 219.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Does it matter if I talk? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.31,
      "end_seconds": 243.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Yes, so don't. Take a deep breath in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.92,
      "end_seconds": 247.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Sorry. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.08,
      "end_seconds": 257.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Your lungs are clear, and your heart sounds are normal, no murmur that I can hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.41,
      "end_seconds": 265.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Marvellous. So what do you think it is? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.11,
      "end_seconds": 284.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.19,
      "text": "Breathlessness when you're carrying a heavy load can come from several things, and from what we have so far, I can't rule out early heart failure yet, though it is only a possibility at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.62,
      "end_seconds": 289.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Is that serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.16,
      "end_seconds": 307.52,
      "duration_seconds": 15.36,
      "text": "It might not be anything much, and I don't want to put a label on it before the tests. I'd like to arrange an echocardiogram, an ultrasound of your heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.12,
      "end_seconds": 313.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Like they do for pregnant women? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.75,
      "end_seconds": 327.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.76,
      "text": "Exactly the same machine, yes. And I'd like to take a blood test to check a heart strain marker and your kidney function, since you're on ramipril."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.8,
      "end_seconds": 332.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Do I need to fast? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.96,
      "end_seconds": 340.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "No fasting needed. The surgery will text you when the scan is booked. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.17,
      "end_seconds": 346.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Right. Should I stop carrying the shopping in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.3,
      "end_seconds": 358.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Not stop, but take it in smaller loads, and rest at the postbox if you need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.68,
      "end_seconds": 365.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Postbox it is. Do I come back after the tests? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.95,
      "end_seconds": 376.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Someone from the practice will ring you with the results and we'll agree what to do next. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.53,
      "end_seconds": 384.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Splendid. Thank you, doctor, you've been very kind. ~"
    }
  ]
}
